  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14168483/assets/87d9088567f74124a4af55333306d81d27cf41798a5411445b68ae0c8bc57550.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            A utility pole is located on the edge of Jacob's land, as shown above. The distance from the right edge of Jacob's plot to the pole is $x+1$ meters. Find the distance to the pole from the left edge as a function of $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The required distance is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nmeters.",
  "worked_solution": "In part 1, we found that the length of Jacob's plot is $2x$ meters.\n\nTo find the required distance, we need to subtract polynomials $2x$ and $x+1:$\n\nWe put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x)-(x+1) & = \\\\ 2x-x-1 & = \\\\ (2-1)x-1 & = \\\\ x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
